Scripted diff: /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/node-startup-location-diagnostics.json --apply --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/startup-location-conversion-receipt.json

Formatting: git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style "{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}" HEAD -- src/init/common.cpp

Convert5 lifecycle calls preserving startup ordering, original no-timestamp guard, config-exists/missing/skipped behavior and Info severity. StartupTime remains the existing rendered UTC wall-clock string, with no new clock read or misleading process-start-time mapping. Filesystem and date producer conversions are unchanged; no claim they were deferred. Support adjustment appends StartupTime. The separate software/chain branding message remains intentionally excluded for the identity owner.

New owned-node functional regression checks real startup height, UTC text, active/default data paths and actual config path after clean shutdown/async flush. Ruff0.15.8, source event lint398 and diff checks pass. Native/functional execution pending a new exact-source gate, separate from validated171.

